  <div class="viewport">
    <main class="stage" id="stage">

      <!-- 00 · Cover -->
      <section class="slide cover" data-title="Cansu Tecimer" data-group="Intro">
        <h1>Cansu Tecimer</h1>
        <p class="body">Product design case studies</p>
        <nav class="case-links">
          <a href="#steady">01 / Steady</a>
          <a href="#gyg">02 / GetYourGuide</a>
        </nav>
        <img class="strip" src="/review/cover-phones.png" alt="" />
        <aside class="notes-src" hidden>
          <ul>
            <li>Two levels of the same craft. Steady: hands-on interaction design. GetYourGuide: product direction and alignment.</li>
            <li>GYG: a team with lots of ideas but nothing cohesive; helped it land on a direction that built trust with executives.</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <!-- Steady 1 · Intro -->
      <section class="slide case-cover" id="steady" data-title="Steady" data-group="Steady">
        <div class="kicker">Case study 01 / Selected work</div>
        <h2>Steady</h2>
        <p class="sub">Designing and building an AI cycling coach for cyclists with specific goals.</p>
        <img class="cover-phone" src="/images/Steady-App-Mobile-Today.png" alt="Steady Today screen on mobile" />
        <div class="hand hand-note">Building an AI native product<br />from scratch.</div>
        <aside class="notes-src" hidden>
          <ul>
            <li>AI coach for cyclists training towards a specific goal. Built with my partner; pilot with three engaged users. Exploration, not validated at scale.</li>
            <li>My role: designed the web app from zero and the brand; built parts of the frontend and the whole marketing site with Claude Code.</li>
            <li>Partner: exercise science, performance logic, backend.</li>
            <li>Principle we arrived at: numbers, metrics, rules and training plans come from deterministic logic. The AI interprets context, writes and narrates the coaching, makes it personal.</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <!-- Steady 2 · The app -->
      <section class="slide lavender" id="steady-app" data-title="Steady, at a glance" data-group="Steady">
        <div class="meta"><span>Steady</span><span>Product overview</span></div>
        <h2 class="title">Steady, at a glance.</h2>
        <div class="overview">
          <figure><img src="/images/Steady-App-Mobile-Today.png" alt="Today screen" /><figcaption>Today</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><img src="/images/Steady-App-Mobile-Schedule.png" alt="Schedule screen" /><figcaption>Schedule</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><img src="/images/Steady-App-Mobile-PlanBlock.png" alt="Plan overview screen" /><figcaption>Overview</figcaption></figure>
          <figure><img src="/images/Steady-App-Mobile-Progress.png" alt="Progress screen" /><figcaption>Progress</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
        <aside class="notes-src" hidden>
          <ul>
            <li>Today · Schedule (each workout, coach feedback after the ride) · Overview of the training block · Progress · and most importantly the coach chat.</li>
            <li>Coaching text over raw numbers. Calm, minimal UI so the coaching stands out.</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <!-- Steady 3 · Onboarding opener -->
      <section class="slide opener" id="steady-onb" data-title="Deep dive: onboarding" data-group="Steady">
        <div class="meta"><span>Steady</span><span>Onboarding</span></div>
        <div class="kicker">Steady / Design deep dive</div>
        <h2>Onboarding</h2>
        <p>How do we take advantage of the personalized, conversational experience an LLM can create without sacrificing the efficiency and control of traditional interaction patterns?</p>
        <aside class="notes-src" hidden>
          <ul>
            <li>We wanted onboarding to feel personal and conversational, but kept running into problems with the LLM.</li>
            <li>So: how do we get that feel without losing the efficiency and control of forms?</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <!-- Steady · Onboarding evolution -->
      <section class="slide" id="steady-onboarding" data-title="Onboarding: three interaction models" data-group="Steady">
